## SQ-MCL-01 | mob cap level mixins
@group A
@commands Boot; `grep -i -E "MobCap|Mixin.*(error|fail)" logs/latest.log`
@pass No mixin error; server reaches `Done`
@fails Name the mixin; SRG ids m_8490_ (tickChunks), m_186524_ (createState), m_186548_ / m_186522_ (cap reads), m_47045_ / m_220421_ (NaturalSpawner)
@from batches/r1031/a1_boot.qb passed
bootreject (?i)(MobCapLevelTickMixin|MobCapMixin|MobCapSpawnAreaMixin).*(error|fail)

## SQ-MCL-02 | one player at night: level 0, about 289 chunks
@group A
@commands One player, night, `/cdevperf mobcap`
@pass overworld about 289 spawnable chunks, level 0; monster count reaches about 70 as vanilla
@fails Level above 0 alone: chunk count read wrong
@from batches/r1031/a2_variants.qb
# self-contained since r1118 (judge-3, 2026-11-18): bot spawn from r1101 p1_server / r1031 a1_world, a2_variants bot row
> execute unless entity qa run pbot spawn qa 0 -60 0 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> tp qa 0 -60 0
> time set 18000
sleep 90
# /ceperf -> /cdevperf since r1118 (judge-8, 2026-11-18): the old root is gone (IDS-02)
> cdevperf mobcap
look overworld about 289 spawnable chunks, level 0; monster count climbing toward vanilla 70

## SQ-MCL-03 | two players 600 apart: level 1, back to 0 together
@group A
@commands Two bots 600 apart, `/cdevperf mobcap`; then bring them together
@pass Apart: about 578 chunks, level 1; together: back to level 0 once below 400
@fails Level does not drop: hysteresis bug
@from batches/r1031/a2_variants.qb
> pbot spawn qb 600 -60 0
sleep 20
> cdevperf mobcap
> tp qb 20 -60 0
sleep 30
> cdevperf mobcap
look apart about 578 chunks and level 1; together back to level 0 once below 400
> pbot remove qb

## SQ-MCL-04 | forced level 2: hostiles settle near 25, none far out
@group A
@commands `mobCapForceLevel 2`, one player at night, `/kill @e[type=!player]`, wait 2 min, `/execute if entity @e[type=minecraft:zombie]` style counts for the common hostiles, then `/tp @p @e[type=minecraft:zombie,sort=furthest,limit=1]` and read the distance moved
@pass Hostiles settle near 25 (not 70); the farthest is no more than about 5 chunks (80 to 90 blocks) from where the player stood
@fails About 70: cap redirect did not apply; far spawns: radius check off
@from batches/r1031/a2_variants.qb
# needs [perf] mobCapForceLevel = 2 set in the toml BEFORE the boot (a running server does not reload the toml);
# run on its own restart (A2: after a2_variants; B1: on the B1b boot), then set it back to -1
sleep 10
# a fresh boot spawns nothing near a just-joined bot for about 2.5 min (seen 2026-10-31, level 0 too): wait it out
sleep 160
> tp qa 0 -60 0
> time set 18000
> kill @e[type=!minecraft:player]
sleep 120
> cdevperf mobcap
> execute if entity @e[type=minecraft:zombie]
> execute if entity @e[type=minecraft:skeleton]
> execute if entity @e[type=minecraft:spider]
> execute if entity @e[type=minecraft:creeper]
> execute as @e[type=#zq:monsters,limit=1,sort=furthest] run data get entity @s Pos
look the four counts sum to about 25 (not 70); the farthest monster within about 90 blocks of 0 0 (perf.md 17); the toml switch is read live (if the level line still says auto, it is not)

## SQ-MCL-05 | forced level 2: no new monster more than 32 blocks above or below the player
@group A
@commands `mobCapForceLevel 2`, player on the surface over deep caves, wait 2 min, `/execute as @e[type=#forge:monsters,distance=..128] run data get entity @s Pos[1]`
@pass No new monster more than 32 blocks above or below the player
@fails Deep cave spawns: band mixin did not apply
@from batches/r1031/b1_gameplay.qb
# r1118 R4 A2 (2026-11-18): [perf] mobCapForceLevel = 2 needs a boot (a running server does not reload it): edit and
# restart in the row, back to -1 at the end; PL is located here (it came from a setup row that was not migrated)
edit python3 "$INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py" toml config/creativeworldgen-common.toml perf mobCapForceLevel 2
restart
> locate biome minecraft:plains
waitlog nearest minecraft:plains is at 120
capture PL nearest minecraft:plains is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> pbot spawn qm {PL1} 120 {PL3} minecraft:overworld survival
# fresh boot: nothing spawns near a just-joined bot for about 2.5 min (2026-10-31): wait it out
sleep 160
> time set 18000
> kill @e[type=#zq:monsters]
sleep 120
> execute at qm as @e[type=#zq:monsters,distance=..128] run data get entity @s Pos[1]
> execute at qm run data get entity qm Pos[1]
look every monster Y within 32 of qm's Y; qm stands in plains over caves
> pbot remove qm
> time set noon
edit python3 "$INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py" toml config/creativeworldgen-common.toml perf mobCapForceLevel -1
restart

